    {
      "id": "all-unbound-visible-rows",
      "profile": "sparql11-query-over-rdf12",
      "kind": "query-evaluation",
      "query": "all-unbound-visible-rows.rq",
      "expected": "all-unbound-visible-rows.srj",
      "data": [
        {
          "path": "data.ttl"
        }
      ],
      "categories": [
        "unbound",
        "schema",
        "multiplicity"
      ],
      "rationale": "VALUES supplies two distinct local mappings. Projection names never, which is unbound in both; both empty visible bindings remain, and the declared never column remains even though no cell binds.",
      "specifications": [
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#inline-data",
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#sparqlAlgebra"
      ],
      "family": "empty-bindings",
      "iri": "http://example.org/community/sparql/interactions/manifest.ttl#all-unbound-visible-rows",
      "manifest": "manifest.ttl"
    },
    {
      "id": "duplicate-unbound-rows",
      "profile": "sparql11-query-over-rdf12",
      "kind": "query-evaluation",
      "query": "duplicate-unbound-rows.rq",
      "expected": "duplicate-unbound-rows.srj",
      "data": [
        {
          "path": "data.ttl"
        }
      ],
      "categories": [
        "unbound",
        "VALUES",
        "duplicate",
        "multiplicity"
      ],
      "rationale": "The VALUES table contains two empty mappings. Bag cardinality is two and both declared columns are unbound. A grader that creates only edges for bound values would erase both rows and is invalid.",
      "specifications": [
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#inline-data",
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#sparqlAlgebra"
      ],
      "family": "empty-bindings",
      "iri": "http://example.org/community/sparql/interactions/manifest.ttl#duplicate-unbound-rows",
      "manifest": "manifest.ttl"
    },
    {
      "id": "bnode-fresh-per-call",
      "profile": "sparql11-query-over-rdf12",
      "kind": "query-evaluation",
      "query": "bnode-fresh-per-call.rq",
      "expected": "bnode-fresh-per-call.srj",
      "data": [
        {
          "path": "data.ttl"
        }
      ],
      "categories": [
        "BNODE",
        "freshness",
        "global-blank-bijection"
      ],
      "rationale": "Every argument-free BNODE invocation creates a fresh node. Two calls for each of two mappings produce four pairwise distinct blanks. The visible a/b keys identify each mapping, so independent per-row blank renaming cannot excuse cross-row aliasing.",
      "specifications": [
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#func-bnode"
      ],
      "family": "bnode-identity",
      "iri": "http://example.org/community/sparql/interactions/manifest.ttl#bnode-fresh-per-call",
      "manifest": "manifest.ttl"
    },
    {
      "id": "bnode-string-memo",
      "profile": "sparql11-query-over-rdf12",
      "kind": "query-evaluation",
      "query": "bnode-string-memo.rq",
      "expected": "bnode-string-memo.srj",
      "data": [
        {
          "path": "data.ttl"
        }
      ],
      "categories": [
        "BNODE",
        "memo",
        "freshness",
        "global-blank-bijection"
      ],
      "rationale": "In one solution mapping equal simple-literal BNODE arguments yield the same blank, so first equals again. Different literal a/b arguments and fresh argument-free calls produce four distinct identities across the two mappings. Equality must hold globally across the entire result bag, including repeated occurrences.",
      "specifications": [
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#func-bnode"
      ],
      "family": "bnode-identity",
      "iri": "http://example.org/community/sparql/interactions/manifest.ttl#bnode-string-memo",
      "manifest": "manifest.ttl"
    },
    {
      "id": "global-blank-cycle",
      "profile": "sparql11-query-over-rdf12",
      "kind": "query-evaluation",
      "query": "global-blank-cycle.rq",
      "expected": "global-blank-cycle.srj",
      "data": [
        {
          "path": "blank-cycle.ttl"
        }
      ],
      "categories": [
        "blank",
        "co-reference",
        "global-blank-bijection"
      ],
      "rationale": "The source graph has two distinct blanks linked in both directions. There are exactly two rows and one global bijection: the from of one row is the to of the other. Four independently renamed nodes across the two rows are not equivalent.",
      "specifications": [
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#queryDataset",
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#sparqlAlgebra"
      ],
      "family": "global-blank-cycle",
      "iri": "http://example.org/community/sparql/interactions/manifest.ttl#global-blank-cycle",
      "manifest": "manifest.ttl"
    },
    {
      "id": "separate-source-blank-scopes",
      "profile": "sparql11-query-over-rdf12",
      "kind": "query-evaluation",
      "query": "separate-source-blank-scopes.rq",
      "expected": "separate-source-blank-scopes.srj",
      "data": [
        {
          "path": "scope1.ttl",
          "graph": "http://example.org/g1"
        },
        {
          "path": "scope2.ttl",
          "graph": "http://example.org/g2"
        }
      ],
      "categories": [
        "source-scope",
        "GRAPH",
        "blank",
        "identity"
      ],
      "rationale": "Each graph file is a distinct RDF source, so its explicit same label identifies a different blank. Graph and literal values identify the rows, and a global result bijection must keep the two blanks distinct.",
      "specifications": [
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#queryDataset",
        "https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql11-query/#sparqlAlgebra"
      ],
      "family": "separate-source-blank-scopes",
      "iri": "http://example.org/community/sparql/interactions/manifest.ttl#separate-source-blank-scopes",
